kingUrn":"urn:li:jobPosting:4372304929","jobState":"LISTED","*jobWorkplaceTypes":["urn:li:fsd_workplaceType:1"],"description":{"textDirection":"USER_LOCALE","text":"Senior Backend Engineer – System Owner (Pegasus SaaS)Location: Northmead (Sydney), NSW, Australia Work Type: Full-time, Onsite Compensation: Competitive market-based remuneration (aligned with senior-level experience and responsibility) About PegasusPegasus is a clinical workflow and pathology logistics SaaS platform designed to manage specimen collection, transport, chain-of-custody, and tracking across hospitals and laboratories.The platform is evolving from a single-site implementation into a scalable, configurable system capable of supporting multiple laboratories and hospitals nationally.This is not a maintenance role. This is a system-owner role.You will take architectural ownership of a real-world clinical system operating at the intersection of healthcare, logistics, and intelligent workflow automation. \nThe RoleWe are seeking a Senior Backend Engineer to take long-term ownership of the Pegasus backend architecture and workflow engine.You will work directly with the Founder/Product Owner and a focused engineering team to design and build a robust, configurable platform that can operate reliably across multiple laboratory environments without manual intervention.This role suits an engineer who enjoys building structured systems properly from first principles — not patching legacy code. Key ResponsibilitiesSystem Architecture & OwnershipOwn backend architecture, database schema design, and API contractsDesign scalable, configurable workflow and rules enginesConvert hard-coded logic into structured, data-driven configuration systemsEnsure system reliability, auditability, and maintainabilityEngineering & DeliveryBuild and maintain APIs and core backend servicesOversee integrations with OCR, voice, and AI componentsParticipate in deployment, monitoring, and incident resolutionMaintain high engineering and documentation standardsSecurity & ComplianceImplement strong access control and auditabilityEnsure system design aligns with healthcare compliance environments (NATA, ISO, CAP principles)Maintain secure handling of sensitive clinical and operational dataLeadershipMentor junior developers and guide technical standardsCollaborate closely with Founder/Product Owner on architecture and roadmapProvide technical direction in a focused, high-trust environmentMentor developers in reviewing, refining, and safely incorporating AI/LLM-assisted code into production systems \nRequired ExperienceEssential5+ years backend development experienceStrong relational database design experience (PostgreSQL preferred)Proven API design experience Experience building configurable/data-driven systemsAbility to make sound architectural decisions in a small, focused teamStrong understanding of security, auditability, and structured system designHighly RegardedHealthcare, laboratory, or logistics systems experienceAWS cloud environment experienceIntegration with OCR, voice, or AI servicesContainerisation (Docker) and modern deployment practices Why This Role Is DifferentTrue system ownership — not a small module inside a large corporationBuild a platform designed to scale nationallyWork directly with the Founder and core decision-makersSolve complex real-world workflow and traceability problemsSmall, focused, high-trust engineering environmentLong-term strategic role with growth as the platform scales \nOnsite RequirementThis role is full-time onsite in Northmead, Sydney.Due to the nature of the system (clinical workflows, sensitive data, and core IP), onsite work is required to ensure:Strong security and IP protectionCompliance with healthcare and audit standardsClose collaboration on architecture and system decisionsRapid response during critical development phasesRemote work is not supported for this role. \nHow to ApplyPlease send:Your resumeA brief note describing a system or platform you have built that you are most proud ofWhy you enjoy building structured, scalable backend systemsEmail: chandraratnam@austpath.com.au\n","attributesV2":[{"start":0,"length":53,"detailData":{"jobPostingName":null,"hyperlink":null,"profileFamiliarName":null,"color":null,"companyName":null,"icon":null,"epoch":null,"systemImage":null,"textLink":null,"listItemStyle":null,"groupName":null,"hyperlinkOpenExternally":null,"listStyle":null,"profileFullName":null,"stringFieldReference":null,"learningCourseName":null,"profileMention":null,"style":"BOLD","schoolName":null,"hashtag":null},"$recipeTypes":["com.linkedin.a86ec3a7ab50c2c801e0395a86ff19c0"],"$type":"com.linkedin.voyager.dash.common.text.TextAttribute"},{"start":0,"length":53,"detailData":{"jobPostingName":null,"hyperlink":null,"profileFamiliarName":null,"color":null,"companyName":null,"icon":null,"epoch":null,"systemImage":null,"textLink":null,"listItemStyle":null,"groupName":null,"hyperlinkOpenExternally":null,"listStyle":null,"profileFullName":null,"stringFieldReference":null,"learningCourseName":null,"profileMention":null,"style":"PARAGRAPH","schoolName":null,"hashtag":null},"$recipeTypes":["com.linkedin.a86ec3a7ab50c2c801e0395a86ff19c0"],"$type":"com.linkedin.voyager.dash.common.text.TextAttribute"},{"start":53,"length":44,"detailData":{"jobPostingName":null,"hyperlink":null,"profileFamiliarName":null,"color":null,"companyName":null,"icon":null,"epoch":null,"systemImage":null,"textLink":null,"listItemStyle":null,"groupName":null,"hyperlinkOpenExternally":null,"listStyle":null,"profileFullName":null,"stringFieldReference":null,"learningCourseName":null,"profileMention":null,"style":"PARAGRAPH","schoolName":null,"hashtag":null},"$recipeTypes":["com.linkedin.a86ec3a7ab50c2c801e0395a86ff19c0"],"$type":"com.linkedin.voyager.dash.common.text.TextAttribute"},{"start":97,"length":29,"detailData":{"jobPostingName":null,"hyperlink":null,"profileFamiliarName":null,"color":null,"companyName":null,"icon":null,"epoch":nul